# The SlopOS crate-ports pin.
#
# `scripts/make_rustc_src.sh` unpacks each crate below from its `.crate`
# (checksum-verified, registry cache first) into the rustc source tree's
# `slopos-crates/<name>-<version>/`, applies `<name>-<version>.patch` there,
# stages the libc fork (`toolchain/libc/`, pinned in `toolchain/PIN`) beside
# them as `slopos-crates/libc/`, and applies `wiring/` at the tree's root.
# `scripts/check_toolchain_pin.sh` fails if any line here stops describing
# what is on disk.
#
# Each port is the PR its crate wants: `target_os = "slopos"` joins the arms
# upstream already has for Linux, Redox or the BSDs wherever SlopOS's libc
# (Linux's layouts, numbers and names) is what those arms assume, plus the
# check-cfg entry a crate carries for a target_os rustc does not know yet.
# Only the versions the compiler and cargo build for a SlopOS host are here,
# measured with `cargo tree --target x86_64-unknown-slopos -e normal,no-proc-macro`
# over `rustc-main`, `rustdoc-tool` and `cargo --no-default-features`:
#
#   getrandom 0.2.17, 0.4.3   cargo           libc `getrandom` backend
#   getrandom 0.3.3           rustc, rustdoc  libc `getrandom` backend
#   libloading 0.9.0          rustc           RTLD_* values
#   nix 0.30.1 (via ctrlc)    rustc           Linux errno table and signal set
#   rustix 1.1.2, 1.1.4       rustc / cargo   ioctl opcode type
#   errno 0.3.14              both            `__errno_location`
#   stacker 0.1.21            rustdoc         `pthread_getattr_np` stack limit
#
# getrandom 0.2.16 and 0.4.3 in rustc's lock, 0.3.4 in cargo's, and nix
# 0.31.3 are locked but never built for the SlopOS host, so they stay
# unpatched.
#
# `wiring/` edits both workspaces' `[patch.crates-io]` and their lockfiles:
# the ports and the libc fork resolve from `slopos-crates/`, and cargo's libc
# moves from 0.2.186 to the fork's 0.2.189. Bootstrap builds tools against the
# tree's own locks, so the lock edits are pinned here rather than regenerated.
